$INCLUDEONCE
' ============================================================================
'  engine/_ALL.BM -- every ENGINE body, in one include. Put this at the BOTTOM.
'
'  ORDER DOES NOT MATTER for correctness: QB64 resolves all SUBs/FUNCTIONs globally, and
'  no body file declares anything at file scope (no DIM SHARED, no file-scope CONST or
'  TYPE -- those all live in the .BI headers, which is what makes this roll-up safe).
'  The order below is for READING: pure utilities, then world, then presentation, then the
'  vendored modules last, matching their own "bodies at the bottom" contract.
' ============================================================================
'$INCLUDE:'TEXT.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'TABLE.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'GAUGE.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'LAYOUT.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'DATA.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'ARTPACK.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'BOARD.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'CURSOR.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'GESTURE.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'JUICE.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'MARKDOWN.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'MUSIC.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'SAVEIO.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'STATS.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'UI.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'DICE3D_GAME.bas'
'$INCLUDE:'DICE3D/_ALL.BM'
'$INCLUDE:'ansi/ANSIPrint.bas'
